==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|happily}}, {{m|enm|happyly}}, {{m|enm|happyliche}}, {{m|enm|happylyche}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|happy|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhæpɪli/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhæpəli/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-happily.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{homophones|en|aptly|aa=in some <<h-dropping>> accents}}
* {{hyphenation|en|hap|pi|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|more|er|comp2_qual=rare|sup2_qual=rare}}

# In a [[happy]] or [[cheerful]] manner; with [[happiness]].
#: {{syn|en|cheerfully|joyously|Thesaurus:happily}}
#::''This time next month I’ll be '''happily''' fishing at the beach.''
#* {{RQ:Defoe Crusoe|page=311|text=And thus I have given the first part of a life of fortune and adventure, a life of Providence's chequer-work, and of a variety which the world will seldom be able to shew the like of: beginning foolishly, but closing much more '''happily''' than any part of it ever gave me leave so much as to hope for.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024 February 21|author=Nick Brodrick|title=Inclusion and development for all|journal=RAIL|issue=1003|page=62|text=Train operating companies get plenty of column inches in the tabloids, usually for negative reasons. '''Happily''', Southeastern is worthy of praise for having made ''The Sun'' for something positive.}}
# By good chance; [[fortunately]], [[successfully]].
#* {{RQ:Beckett Watt|text=Watt wore, on his feet, a boot, brown in colour, and a shoe, '''happily''' of a brownish colour also.}}
# With good will; in all happiness; [[willingly]].
#: {{syn|en|gladly}}
#: {{ux|en|I will '''happily''' help you look for your lost wallet.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[by chance|By chance]]; [[perhaps]].
#: {{syn|en|haply}}
#* {{RQ:Montaigne Florio Essayes|chapter=12|book=II|passage=And who knoweth whether a thousand yeares hence a third opinion will rise, which '''happily''' shall overthrow these two precedents?}}

